# ============================================================================
# Privacy Shield — Anti-fingerprinting Blink patch
# Injection points: canvas (getImageData/toDataURL/toBlob/webgl), webrtc
# (port allocator), navigator (hardwareConcurrency/platform/userAgent).
#
# Consolidated from the adversarial-reviewer-CORRECTED diffs for all three
# points. Cross-patch conflicts resolved by the orchestrator:
#   * features.h / features.cc: kFarbleCanvas, kFarbleWebRTC, kSpoofNavigator
#     are each DECLARED once and DEFINED once (the three source patches each
#     tried to emit them -> would be a duplicate-symbol/ODR link error).
#   * Session-token switch UNIFIED to --antidetect-session-token across all
#     three readers (writer drafts used myapp-session-token in canvas/webrtc
#     and antidetect-session-token in navigator). One browser-appended switch
#     now drives every hook: canvas parses it as a uint64 HMAC seed; webrtc and
#     navigator gate on presence.
#
# *** NOT COMPILED. *** Hook-body hunks use APPROXIMATE context (the writers had
# no live Chromium tree). This will NOT `git apply` clean as-is. Apply with:
#     git apply --recount --reject privacy-shield-antidetect.patch
# then hand-place every *.rej against the actual milestone. New files apply
# cleanly; the 8 hook hunks and the BUILD.gn/DEPS hunks need reconciliation.
# See the `verification` section for the full unverified-symbol list.
# ============================================================================

